            <h2>Definition</h2>
            <ul>
              <li> A <code>search</code> landmark contains a collection of items and objects that, as a whole, combine to create search functionality to content on the website.</li>
              <li> ARIA 1.2 Specification: <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#search"><code>search</code> landmark</a></li>
            </ul>
            <h2>Design Patterns</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>Use the <code>search</code> landmark instead of the <code>form</code> landmark when the form is used for search functionality.</li>
              <li>If a page includes more than one <code>search</code> landmark, each should have a unique label.</li>
            </ul>
            <section aria-label="Coding Techniques">
              <ul id="myTabs" class="nav nav-tabs" role="tablist">
                <li class="nav-item" role="none">
                  <a class="nav-link" id="tab2" href="#tabpanel2" aria-controls="tabpanel2" role="tab">
                    HTML Techniques
                  </a>
                </li>
                <li class="nav-item" role="none">
                  <a class="nav-link" id="tab1" href="#tabpanel1" aria-controls="tabpanel1" role="tab">
                    ARIA Techniques
                  </a>
              </ul>
              <div class="tab-content">
                <div id="tabpanel2" aria-labelledby="tab2" role="tabpanel" class="tab-pane active">

                    {% include "./landmark-search.njk" %}

                  <h3>HTML Example</h3>
                  <search>
                    <input type="search" size="20" aria-label="search text"><input type="submit" value="Search">
                  </search>
                  <br>
                  <div class="code">
                    <code>
                    <strong>&lt;search&gt;</strong>
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;input type="search" aria-label="search text" size="20"&gt;
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;input type="submit" value="Search"&gt;
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    <strong>&lt;/search&gt;</strong>
                    <br>
                    </code>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div id="tabpanel1" aria-labelledby="tab1" role="tabpanel" class="tab-pane">
                  <p>A <code>role="search"</code> attribute is used to define a <code>search</code> landmark.</p>
                  <h3>ARIA Example</h3>

                  <form role="search">

                  <input type="search" size="20" aria-label="search text"><input type="submit" value="Search">

                  </form>

                  <div class="code">
                    <code>
                    &lt;form <strong>role="search"</strong>&gt;
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;input type="search" aria-label="search text" size="20"&gt;
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;input type="submit" value="Search"&gt;
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    &lt;/form&gt;
                    <br>
                    </code>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </section>
